37. INTERVIEW EXPLANATION
==================================================

QUESTION:

Explain your project.


ANSWER:

"In this project, I deployed a Java web application on an AWS EC2
Ubuntu server.

I installed Java 21 and Tomcat 10 using the Ubuntu APT package
manager. I deployed the Java WAR application into Tomcat's webapps
directory.

For frontend traffic, I installed Nginx and configured it as a
reverse proxy. Nginx listens on port 80 and forwards requests to
Tomcat running on localhost port 8080.

I also configured and managed Tomcat using systemd, monitored Nginx
and Tomcat logs, and created a Bash deployment script to simplify
WAR deployment.

For security, I exposed only SSH and HTTP through the EC2 Security
Group and kept Tomcat port 8080 private.

I also tested failure scenarios such as stopping Tomcat and
troubleshooting the resulting 502 Bad Gateway error."


